            "disclaimer_ucs":"The data on conservation areas used in these statistics cover all categories: federal, state and municipal. These areas were last updated in 2022, and a new update will be carried out soon. For further details on the source data, please consult the <br><a target='_blank' style='color: blue;' href='https://terrabrasilis.dpi.inpe.br/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/62c97440-507d-4002-868d-3379050bce03'>metadata</a>.",
            "warning_rates":"New data.<br>Estimated deforestation rates in the Brazilian Legal Amazon for 2025/2026 period based on 271 priority tiles.<br><a target='_blank' style='color: blue;' href='https://data.inpe.br/biomasbr/notas-tecnicas/'>Learn more at technical note.</a>",
            "warning_increase":"See the new deforestation increment data for the Brazilian Legal Amazon and Amazon Biome for the 2025/2026 period, measured based on 271 priority tiles.",
            "addMask":"<h3>Aggregated Data</h3><p>The aggregated data are composed of the sum of the <em>accumulated mask</em> and the <em>deforestation residues</em>, representing the total consolidated deforested area over time.</p><h3>Change in the charts display</h3><p>When this option is enabled, the deforestation increment charts start showing the <em>aggregated data</em> instead of the annual increments.</p><p>In this visualization mode, each year represents the <em>total accumulated deforestation</em> up to that period. The value of a given year is obtained by summing the accumulated total of the previous year with the increment recorded in the current year.</p><p>As a consequence, the values no longer represent only the annual increment and start representing the accumulated deforestation up to each year.</p><h3>Year filter behavior</h3><p>Since the values are cumulative, each group (Group 1 and Group 2) allows the selection of <em>only one year at a time</em>.</p><p>To compare two periods, select one year in Group 1 and another year in Group 2. The <em>Deforestation increment - filter sensitive</em> card will display the accumulated value of each group.</p>"
